@startuml BudgetDarpanSystemContext
!include _theme.puml
title Budget Darpan — System Context and Core Use Cases
caption AI-powered civic transparency with traceable public evidence
left to right direction

actor Citizen
actor "Verified Citizen" as Verified
actor "Municipal Official" as Official
actor "Journalist / Researcher" as Researcher
actor "Moderator / Admin" as Admin

rectangle "Budget Darpan" as System #E8F4F1 {
  usecase "Explore budgets\nand projects" as UC1
  usecase "Follow project\nmoney trail" as UC2
  usecase "Ask in English, Nepali\nor Romanized Nepali" as UC3
  usecase "Open cited document\nand page" as UC4
  usecase "Inspect maps\nand charts" as UC5
  usecase "Understand anomaly\nreason and threshold" as UC6
  usecase "Verify identity\nwith mock provider" as UC7
  usecase "Submit or edit one\nproject rating" as UC8
  usecase "Review OCR and\nmoderate evidence" as UC9
}

cloud "Official public sources\nMunicipal sites · OAG · e-GP" as Sources BLUESOFT
rectangle "Mock identity provider\nNot official Nagarik App" as MockID #FFF1C5

Citizen --> UC1
Citizen --> UC2
Citizen --> UC3
Citizen --> UC4
Citizen --> UC5
Citizen --> UC6
Verified --> UC7
Verified --> UC8
Researcher --> UC1
Researcher --> UC3
Researcher --> UC4
Official --> UC2
Official --> UC6
Admin --> UC9

Sources --> System : budget, audit, tender,\nprogress and payment evidence
UC7 --> MockID : signed demo assertion
UC8 .> UC7 : requires verification
UC3 .> UC4 : cited claims

note bottom of System
  Public inspection requires no login.
  Exact money comes from structured data.
  Missing evidence stays Unknown, never zero.
end note

legend right
  |= Trust boundary |= Meaning |
  | Official source | Government-published evidence |
  | Mock identity | Hackathon security demonstration |
  | AI answer | Evidence-bounded, not an accusation |
endlegend
@enduml
